// printf — daily-ten 18 Nov 2026 (OS track).
// Simulates `printf "%d %f %s"`: prints an int (42),
// a float (3.5), and a string ("hi"), each on its own
// line (str + int concatenation is not supported), then
// the value count (3).
fn main() {
    println(42);
    println(3.5);
    println("hi");
    println(3);
}
